AB  - In order to produce weanling rats with low levels of n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids in their body lipids, a stock diet and a purified diet with very high linoleic acid/.alpha.-linolenic acid ratios were formulated. These diets contained 10% and 15% sunflower oil, and 0,32 and 0,21 g/kg .alpha.-linolenic acid, respectively. Female rats from two Wistar strains were fed these diets from weaning through growth, gestation and lactation. A commercial stock diet was used for comparison. The litters from one strain fed the purified diet had a moderate but significant perinatal mortality. Satisfactory growth and reproduction performances were observed in both strains with the stock diet.
