T2  - 14TH WORLD CONGRESS ON CLINICAL NUTRITION AND 5TH INTERNATIONAL CONGRESS ON CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASES
CP  - 14th World Congress of the International College of Nutrition (ICN)/5th Congress of the International College of Cardiology (ICC)
AB  - Although there has been a great progress in the prevention of cardiovascular diseases to date, the mortality of patients with acute myocardial infarction (AMI) still remains high. One of the most important underlying causes explaining this phenomenon is the sudden cardiac death. Hence, there is an urgent medical need for a targeted therapy to reduce the incidence of sudden cardiac death. Results from GISSI Prevenzione Trial show that adding the omega-3 fatty acids (n-3 PUFA) to standard therapy of patients who survived AMI has the ability to reduce sudden cardiac death (44 % risk reduction, p=0,0006). In addition, significant decline in all-cause cardiovascular mortality (21% risk reduction, p=0,0064) further emphasizes the role of n-3 PUFA in cardiovascular prevention. To date, beneficial effects of n-3 PUFA are attributed to their antiarrhythmic, lipid lowering, antithrombotic and anti-inflammatory properties.
