TI  - ω-3 carboxylic acids for hypertriglyceridemia
T2  - EXPERT OPINION ON PHARMACOTHERAPY
AB  - Introduction: omega-3 carboxylic acids (omega 3 CA), also called w3 free fatty acids (omega 3 FFA), with the trade name Epanova (TM) is a new formulation of eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) + docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) approved for the treatment of severe hypertriglyceridemia. The FFA form of EPA and DHA is associated with higher bioavailability than other forms of omega 3 fatty acids, potentially resulting in efficacy at lower doses and less dependence on meal relationship.
   Areas covered: The efficacy and safety of omega 3 CA from clinical trials as well as PK and PD data will be reviewed. The mechanism of action of omega 3 fatty acids in the lowering of triglycerides (TG) will be discussed and comparison is made with omega 3 ethyl ester compounds.
   Expert opinion: omega 3 CA are a unique form of omega 3 fatty acids that appear safe and effective in lowering serum TG and offer the possibility of better patient compliance due to lower-dose efficacy and the ability to take with or without food. omega 3 CA lowered TG by 26 and 31% for the 2 and 4 g/day doses, respectively, and Apo CIII was also lowered 11 and 14%, respectively, as well.
