TI  - Omega 3 fatty acid supplementation and the risk of cardiovascular events
T2  - AGRO FOOD INDUSTRY HI-TECH
AB  - In the last years a growing amount of evidence regarding the cardio-protective role of Omega 3 fatty acids (n-3 PUFA) became progressively appealing. Still the role of n-3 PUFA as a strategy for the prevention of coronary disease remains uncertain. The objective of this review is to analyze the evidence regarding the protective role of n-3 PUFA on coronary heart disease, with particular emphasis on their potential to reduce myocardial infarction. Although the results of experimental studies are heterogeneous, epidemiological data, randomized controlled trials and basic science support their role for the prevention of coronary heart disease. The reduction in mortality seemed to be related to a reduction in fatal MI and sudden death, with no effect on non-fatal MI.
