TI  - Current evidence and future perspectives of omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids for the prevention of cardiovascular disease
T2  - EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF PHARMACOLOGY
AB  - Omega-3 fatty acids have been traditionally used for the prevention of major cardiovascular events in patients with or without a history of cardiovascular disease. Their main mechanism of action is to lower triglyceride levels, but they also exert anti-arrythmic and anti-inflammatory properties, they reduce blood pressure levels and stabilize the atherosclerotic plaques. There is a vast amount of evidence derived from randomized studies that seems to question their benefit for the prevention of major cardiovascular events. Upcoming trials will help to better clarify their use in certain indications. (C) 2013 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.
