TI  - Recent select meta-analyses cast doubt on efficacy of omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids in cardiovascular outcomes
T2  - AGRO FOOD INDUSTRY HI-TECH
AB  - Omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFAs) are commonly consumed for their potential health benefits, one being cardiovascular disease prevention. This article examines the results of recent meta analyses evaluating the cardiovascular benefits of omega-3 PUFAs. The majority of these analyses show mixed results, which has caused some clinicians and patients to question the benefit of omega-3 PUFAs in preventing cardiovascular outcomes. In conclusion, additional clinical trials with adequate study design could help clear up some of the mixed data that is currently published in terms of omega-3 PUFAs and cardiovascular outcomes.
